ta: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1996,VITAMINA D,\"VITAMINA D, also known as Vitamin D, is an essential fat-soluble nutrient crucial for maintaining bone health and regulating calcium and phosphate levels in the body. It plays a significant role in calcium absorption, which is vital for preventing conditions such as osteoporosis, rickets, and osteomalacia. Deficiencies in Vitamin D are common, particularly among older adults, individuals with limited sun exposure, and those with certain health conditions, including chronic kidney disease, cirrhosis, and inflammatory bowel disease. \n\nThe recommended daily intake of Vitamin D varies, with suggestions typically ranging from 400 to 1000 IU, depending on age and health status. For instance, infants, especially those who are exclusively breastfed, are advised to receive a daily supplement of 400 IU to prevent deficiency. In older adults, adequate levels of Vitamin D are essential for maintaining muscle strength and reducing the risk of falls and fractures.\n\nVitamin D can be synthesized in the skin upon exposure to sunlight, but it is also found in dietary sources such as fatty fish, eggs, and fortified dairy products. In certain populations, such as those with obesity or undergoing bariatric surgery, supplementation may be necessary to achieve optimal levels. Additionally, Vitamin D is often monitored in patients receiving parenteral nutrition and those with elevated parathyroid hormone (PTH) levels.\n\nBeyond its role in bone health, Vitamin D has been associated with various other health benefits, including potential protective effects against certain cancers, cardiovascular diseases, and cognitive decline. It is also important for immune function and may influence insulin secretion and glucose metabolism.\n\nIn summary, VITAMINA D is a vital nutrient that supports overall health, particularly bone and muscle function, and is often supplemented in various populations to prevent deficiencies and promote well-being.\",74\r\n14087,ACADÉMIA AMERICANA DE PEDIATRÍA,\"The Academia Americana de Pediatría (AAP) is an organization dedicated to pediatric health, providing essential guidelines and recommendations for various aspects of child care. Among its key contributions, the AAP offers advice on the introduction of solid foods for children at high risk of food allergies, ensuring that parents and caregivers are informed about best practices to promote health and safety. Additionally, since 2008, the AAP has also recommended vitamin D supplementation for children, highlighting its importance in maintaining optimal health during early development. Through these initiatives, the AAP plays a crucial role in guiding pediatric care and supporting the well-being of children.\",2\r\n14411,DIRECCIÓN GENERAL DE SALUD Y PROTECCIÓN DEL CONSUMIDOR,\"The Dirección General de Salud y Protección del Consumidor is a European Commission body that oversees health and consumer protection, including nutritional guidelines.\",2\r\n5686,\"1,25(OH)₂D₃\",\"1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 is the active form of vitamin D that regulates calcium and phosphate metabolism in the body.\",1\r\n5685,25(OH)D,25-hydroxyvitamin D is a form of vitamin D that is measured in the blood to assess vitamin D status.,1\r\n3476,BISCHOFF-FERRARI,Bischoff-Ferrari is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the effects of vitamin D supplementation on fracture reduction.,1\r\n16882,\"DELTIUS 25000 UI/2,5 ML\",\"Deltius 25000 UI/2,5 ml is an oral solution containing 25,000 UI of cholecalciferol (Vitamin D3) per 2.5 ml bottle.\",1\r\n16885,\"HIDROFEROL 0,1 MG/ML\",\"Hidroferol 0,1 mg/ml is an oral solution containing 0.1 mg (100 μg) of calcifediol (6,000 UI of 25-OH-Vitamin D3) per ml.\",1\r\n16884,HIDROFEROL CHOQUE 3 MG,\"Hidroferol Choque 3 mg is