nts discussed in the context of supplementation and health recommendations,100\r\n8392,VITAMINA D,ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES,\"La vitamina D se asocia con la mejora de la salud cardiovascular y la regulación de la glucosa, lo que puede influir en la aparición de enfermedades cardiovasculares. Además, se ha observado que niveles adecuados de vitamina D están relacionados con un menor riesgo de desarrollar estas enfermedades, indicando una conexión significativa entre la vitamina D y la salud cardiovascular.\",96\r\n8391,VITAMINA D,SÍNDROME METABÓLICO,\"La vitamina D y el síndrome metabólico están interrelacionados, ya que la hipovitaminosis D se asocia con un mayor riesgo de desarrollar síndrome metabólico. Además, se sugiere que la vitamina D puede tener un efecto protector sobre esta condición, lo que indica una relación significativa entre ambos.\",95\r\n7156,TRASPLANTE HEPÁTICO,VITAMINA D,Vitamin D supplementation is crucial for liver transplant patients to maintain calcium levels,94\r\n8015,FÓSFORO,VITAMINA D,\"FÓSFORO and VITAMINA D are closely related in the context of bone health and mineralization. The deficiency of vitamina D leads to hipofosfatemia, which is characterized by low levels of phosphorus in the blood. This condition arises due to a decreased absorption of phosphorus in the intestines. Conversely, vitamina D plays a crucial role in facilitating the absorption of phosphorus in the intestines, making it essential for proper bone mineralization. Thus, adequate levels of vitamina D are vital for maintaining healthy phosphorus levels, which in turn supports overall bone health.\",93\r\n8370,VITAMINA D,INFUVITE PEDIÁTRICO,Infuvite Pediátrico contains Vitamin D as part of its composition for pediatric nutrition,92\r\n8406,VITAMINA D,HIPOCALCEMIA,\"La deficiencia de vitamina D puede llevar a una absorción inadecuada de calcio, contribuyendo a la hipocalcemia.\",92\r\n8394,VITAMINA D,FIBRA DIETÉTICA,Vitamin D and dietary fiber are both important nutrients that have been researched for their effects on health and weight management.,91\r\n8401,VITAMINA D,PACIENTES CIRRÓTICOS,\"Cirrhotic patients often experience vitamin D deficiency, which is prevalent in this population\",91\r\n1913,ENFERMEDAD DE ALZHEIMER,VITAMINA D,La vitamina D puede influir en la salud cognitiva y su deficiencia se ha relacionado con un mayor riesgo de demencia.,90\r\n8387,VITAMINA D,HIPOCALEMIA,Vitamin D is crucial for preventing and treating hypocalcemia by facilitating calcium absorption,89\r\n8395,VITAMINA D,TIAMINA,\"Thiamine and vitamin D deficiencies are both critical concerns in patients post-surgery, requiring careful monitoring and supplementation.\",87\r\n8404,VITAMINA D,CALCITONINA,\"La vitamina D y la calcitonina tienen efectos opuestos en el metabolismo del calcio, donde la vitamina D aumenta la absorción y la calcitonina inhibe la reabsorción ósea.\",83\r\n8367,VITAMINA D,MALNUTRICIÓN EN CÁNCER,Vitamin D is recommended for cancer patients to support overall health and combat malnutrition,82\r\n8384,VITAMINA D,RAQUITISMO,\"VITAMINA D and RAQUITISMO are closely related, particularly in the context of health conditions such as celiac disease. Rickets, a condition characterized by weak and soft bones, is primarily caused by a deficiency in vitamin D. In patients with celiac disease, the malabsorption of vitamin D can contribute to the development of rickets. Therefore, ensuring adequate levels of vitamin D is crucial in preventing rickets, especially in individuals who may have absorption issues due to gastrointestinal disorders.\",82\r\n8410,VITAMINA D,MINERALES Y OLIGOELEMENTOS,Both Vitamin D and minerals are discussed in the context of nutritional support for patients with specific health conditions,82\r\n8403,VITAMINA D,HORMONA PARATIROIDEA,\"La hormona paratiroidea estimula la síntesis de vitamina D, que a su vez incrementa la absorción intestinal de calcio y fósforo.\",81\r\n8381,VITAMINA D,PTH,La deficiencia de vitamina D pu